{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966788,"nonce":"OwSJKqZTBGBh9zRFn/TSyXWTZqQ=","title":"Bare signal reads inside computed{} bodies are never rewritten to getters — rewrite_expr","message":"`computed { \u003csignal\u003e ... }` **never reads the signal**. Confirmed by HIR + CLIF\ndump, not inference. The earlier \"accessor picked from return type\" note was\nwrong.\n\n**Root cause:** `rewrite_expr` in `passes/signals.rs` has **no\n`TypedExpression::Variable` arm**. It rewrites only three shapes:\n\n- `\u003csig\u003e.get()` — MethodCall with a Variable receiver\n- `\u003csig\u003e.field` — Call with a Field callee\n- `\u003csig\u003e = expr` — Assign, special-cased before the recursive walk\n\nA bare `count` inside a computed body is a plain `TypedExpression::Variable`\nand falls through `_ =\u003e {}`. It recurses into Lambda bodies correctly, so the\nwalk is not the problem; the arm is simply missing.\n\n**Two divergent failure modes, same bug.** SSA can't resolve the variable in\neither case, and picks a fallback by whether the name matches a known function:\n\n- name does *not* collide (`busy`) -\u003e \"Not an enum constructor or function,\n  reading as undefined variable\" -\u003e phi with 0 predecessors. **Compiles and\n  links, silently reads undefined.** This is the dangerous one.\n- name *does* collide (`count`) -\u003e \"Variable 'count' is a function - emitting\n  function ref\" -\u003e extern decl -\u003e `can't resolve symbol count` at JIT link.\n\nHIR for the failing case:\n```\nfunction @count() -\u003e opaque(i64) system_v { extern }\nfunction @__lambda_HirId(70)() -\u003e bool fast {\n    %v2 = call funcref @count()     ; should be __signal_get_by_id_i64(\u003cid\u003e)\n    %v3: i64 = gt %v2, %v1\n```\nCLIF shows it degrade further, to a function-address compare:\n```clif\nv2 = func_addr.i64 fn0   ; address of @count\nv3 = icmp sgt v2, v1\n```\n\n**Second, independent gap:** the accessor maps\n(`typed_signal_extern_name` / `typed_signal_setter_extern_name` in\n`passes/signals.rs`, mirrored in `passes/reactive.rs` and `passes/styling.rs`)\ncover **I32, F64, Bool, String only — no I64**. `signal count: i64` has no\naccessor to rewrite to even once the Variable arm exists. `abi.rs` registers\n`__signal_get_by_id_i32` but no i64 form.\n\n**FIXED cb819e3d** via `rewrite_bare_reads`, scoped to lambda bodies (a lambda body is a pure value context; the widget-arg position still needs the bare name as a raw id for `lower_reactive_args`). Lambda params shadow same-named signals; the rewritten node carries the *signal's* type, so `: bool` over an i32 signal reads i32 and compares. Original plan was: add a `Variable` arm that rewrites bare signal reads to\n`__signal_get_by_id_\u003cT\u003e(id)`, and add I64 to the accessor maps + `abi.rs`.\nScope the Variable rewrite carefully: the extern-widget reactive-arg path\n(Shape A'/B in `passes/reactive.rs`) passes the bare signal name expecting the\nraw *id*, not a value read. Restrict to lambda/computed bodies, or order it\nafter `lower_reactive_args`.\n\n**No coverage exists.** No `.blinc` file and no dsl_core test uses `computed`\nat all; the cn_dsl reactive tests only assert `compile_source` succeeds, never\nthe value. Any fix needs a value assertion, not a compile assertion.\n\n**i64 is not a DSL type.** The grammar defines `state_type_i32` but no i64\nrule, so `signal count: i64` never parses as an i64 signal — that was a bad\ntest, not a compiler bug. cb819e3d plumbs the i64 half anyway (SignalType,\nhost externs, abi descriptors, grammar symbol table, three accessor maps); it\nstays unreachable from source until a grammar type rule lands.\n\n**Confirmed working end-to-end** (visual, 2026-07-26): the derived row in\n`crates/blinc_dsl_core/examples/reactive_dsl.blinc` tracks the raw-binding row\non every Step, including a two-source `computed { Ticker.pct + Ticker.radius /\n200.0 } : f64`. All three read shapes lower correctly: bare signal, `.get()`,\nand FSM context field (`Ticker.pct`, a Field access on a separate path).\n\n**Testing note:** `parse_to_typed_ast` exposes an *earlier* pass stage than\n`compile_source`, so a typed-AST `callee_exists` assertion does NOT see this\nrewrite. Verify at the HIR level instead:\n`ZYNTAX_DUMP_HIR=1 RUST_LOG=trace` (needs `tracing_subscriber::fmt::try_init()`\nin the test, or the log is empty). Guard lives at\n`crates/blinc_cn_dsl/tests/cn_button_reactive.rs::cn_button_disabled_computed_bare_signal_read`.\n\nSee project cn reactive prop migration, gotcha dsl computed binding zero,\ngotcha lower reactive args wrapped getter.","files":null}]}